    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0088" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 (D) E.D.B./1974: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-05T19:00:00-04:00">November 5, 1942—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1325. Your 1849, October 30, 1942, 11 p.m.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d87-f1"/> To
                    countries listed in Department’s 1296, October 28, 8 p.m. please add 5.84
                    percent for Uruguay. Department feels that exports from Chile to other American
                    republics in excess of the percentage indicated should be permitted when
                    conditions warrant and when approved by both Chilean and United States
                    Governments.</p>
                <pb facs="0089" n="75" xml:id="pg75"/>
                <p>The Department feels that the percentage basis is the fairest approach for making
                    allocations in order that all the republics may be treated in a similar
                    manner.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
